WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.834
Tonight, Russia

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.835
is being rattled

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.870
by attacks on its own territory,

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.939
as well as a key port city

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.407
in occupied Ukraine.

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:07.774
Our senior

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:08.675
international correspondent

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.709
Sam Kiley is joining us

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.644
live now from eastern Ukraine.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.712
Sam, Russian officials

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.980
trying to reassure

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.182
residents living under Kremlin control,

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:18.785
but these attacks are really intensifying

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.024
they are intensifying attacks in addition

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:24.524
to the one

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.859
you referred to there in Berlin.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.028
There was a drone attack in Smolensk

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:31.831
on an oil refinery or some similar

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.700
type building.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.835
And of course, there have been ongoing

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:37.804
incursions and attacks

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:38.805
much closer to here.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.106
Just north

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:43.309
on the border between Ukraine and Russia.

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:44.010
And it's those,

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:45.912
I think, that have really shaken

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:47.347
the Russians up

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:50.884
here.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.352
A Ukrainian strike in

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.087
Russian occupied by the UNSC

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.824
last summer

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:00.593
in Gloucester, Kharkiv.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:02.662
It's heating up across several fronts

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.730
in Russia.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.031
The governor of Belgorod

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.233
Province struggles to reassure

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.135
a rattled population.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.770
To be honest, kokrokoo.

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:12.272
I heard that the armed forces

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.641
of Ukraine continue to show our territory

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.209
more than 2500

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.143
people are staying

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:17.777
in temporary

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.813
accommodation facilities in Belgorod.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.614
There are many questions

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.083
that residents of Shevchenko

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.884
and border villages are asking.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.120
Starting with Who will pay my utilities?

00:01:27.287 --> 00:01:28.588
What about our property?

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.056
Who is watching over it?

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:31.324
Ukrainian backed Russian

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.759
dissident soldiers claim

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.928
to have raided Russia a second time

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.363
over a slow in a stunt

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.998
that could have been filmed anywhere.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:39.966
One fighter

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.401
displayed a fridge magnet

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.604
from Belgorod on social media, soon due

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:47.373
to will be able to walk in free Belgorod

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:49.843
and then across all Russia.

00:01:49.843 --> 00:01:50.877
He said.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.313
Vladimir Putin has stepped in to steady

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.781
the national nerves

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.316
She wouldn't let a commission move

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.517
across a museum.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:01:57.984
Today,

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:59.853
we will also address these issues

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:00.420
in relation

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.255
to ensuring Russia's security.

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.089
In this case,

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:05.258
domestic political security.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:06.559
Considering the efforts,

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.894
our foes are still taking

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:08.862
and stepping up

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.864
in order to destabilize the situation

00:02:10.864 --> 00:02:11.965
inside Russia,

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.166
we must do everything

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:13.600
we can

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.868
to prevent this from happening

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.302
at any cost to

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.271
the US.

00:02:18.271 --> 00:02:21.107
Setting out some grim truths for Moscow.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:22.142
When you look at

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.309
President Putin's long term

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.145
strategic aims and objectives,

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.347
there is no question.

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.048
Russia is significantly worse off

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.450
today than it was before

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:31.384
its full scale invasion

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:33.686
of Ukraine militarily.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.022
Economically, geopolitically.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:37.924
That's certainly

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.325
the message that Ukraine's

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:41.427
trying to deliver to Russia

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:44.230
and now by force,

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.700
And I think that message

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.402
has been forcefully delivered

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.971
once again with a partizan attack

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.875
claimed by Ukrainian supporters inside

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:57.310
the occupied

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.912
town of Melita Poll

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.346
with the bombing of a car

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.981
killing one so-called

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:02.982
collaborator

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.285
and injuring at least three others.

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:07.086
And we are seeing a lot

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.855
more of these sorts of events,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.323
particularly close

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.558
to that southern front,

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:13.326
where both sides, both the Russians

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.394
and the Ukrainians,

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:15.562
have been pounding each other

00:03:15.562 --> 00:03:17.664
ever more frequently with artillery.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.133
Alex, really a remarkable escalation.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.868
Sam Kiley in Kiev in eastern Ukraine,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.570
thank you very much for that report.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.437
Let's discuss all this

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.639
with CNN contributor of Russian affairs

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.340
Jill Dougherty

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:27.941
and retired

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:29.509
Colonel Cedric Leighton, a CNN

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.743
military analyst.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.078
Thank you both for joining me

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.012
this evening.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:35.348
Jill, I'm really struck by that soundbite

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:36.182
that Sam just played

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:36.749
from Vladimir

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.452
Putin there, assuring his population

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:40.987
that we will do everything

00:03:40.987 --> 00:03:42.088
we can to prevent this

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:43.556
from happening at any cost.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:45.024
He's really having

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.160
to tell the Russian population

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.128
this will be okay.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.630
What do you think he's going to do?

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:51.698
How can he follow through on that?

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.666
Promise? I don't think that he can.

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:55.668
I mean, these attacks are coming.

00:03:56.536 --> 00:03:58.771
They seem incapable of stopping them.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:00.807
I mean, if they could, they would.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.008
But they continue

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.743
And then you have the drone attacks

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.845
just a few days ago in Moscow.

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:08.748
So I think he's got a real problem in

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.550
a lot of

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.185
the way he approaches his don't

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.052
talk about it,

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:13.486
you know,

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.120
but the fact

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.022
that they have that quote today,

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:18.091
he is trying to tell people it's okay,

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:19.092
as he always says,

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:20.093
it's under control,

00:04:20.093 --> 00:04:21.794
but it's not under control.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.030
And those residents certainly feeling

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:25.398
that it's not under control.

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.032
And Cedric,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:27.834
some some dramatic language

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.702
Ukrainians saying that the gates of war

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.037
have now been opened.

00:04:31.037 --> 00:04:34.307
Clearly, these attacks inside Russia are

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:37.110
putting the Kremlin off-balance there.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:38.444
They seem to be rattled as well.

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:39.879
But do you see any downside, any

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:41.281
any risks to this?

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.181
Well, there certainly are.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.816
Alex, I think one of the key things

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.550
that the Ukrainians

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:45.685
have to watch out for

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:46.486
is attacking

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.655
too many civilian targets in Russia.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:49.656
I you know,

00:04:49.656 --> 00:04:50.123
right now

00:04:50.123 --> 00:04:51.457
they're on the moral high ground right?

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:52.358
They own all of that

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.293
because the people

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.927
that are actually attacking

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:56.329
civilian targets are the Russians

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.130
for the most part.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.132
And that has given Ukraine

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:02.135
a lot of support in a material sense

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:03.603
in a diplomatic sense

00:05:03.603 --> 00:05:05.305
and certainly in a military sense.

00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:07.440
And it risks you know,

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.274
Ukraine risks

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.076
something very big here

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.346
if it does something that does not impact

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.114
the military objective directly.

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:15.481
In other words,

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:16.616
if they go into the civilian

00:05:16.616 --> 00:05:17.317
side of things,

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:18.751
so they have to be very careful

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:20.720
to concentrate more on the military side.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.922
And yes, even on the political side.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.390
But the one thing that they have done

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.024
very well

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:26.626
is so distrust

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.226
terror

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.028
in the minds of the Russian population.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.263
The White House has said very clearly

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.164
they would rather

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.598
they not see Ukraine

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.567
striking inside of Russia.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:34.934
Jill,

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.302
it is now very apparent

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.937
to the Russian citizens themselves

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.039
that these strikes are taking place.

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:41.474
You have these attacks

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:42.208
against smaller

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.042
border towns

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.911
in the western part of Russia.

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:45.778
But you also have

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:47.380
these recent drone attacks

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:50.350
near Moscow, including in and around

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:51.584
a neighborhood

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:54.020
that is where some of the elite live.

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:55.621
So to what extent

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.057
do you think the Russian sentiment

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:59.492
about the war is changing

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:01.260
and changing more against it?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:01.561
You know,

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:03.563
I think an interesting part of this

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:04.831
is that

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:07.233
when it's been happening in that town

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:09.235
that we just saw the video from Shabake,

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:09.769
you know,

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:12.271
I mean, that's been hit for months

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:14.273
and nobody really talked about it.

00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:17.243
The people out there feel, hey, you know,

00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.678
you don't talk about it

00:06:18.678 --> 00:06:20.613
until it happens in Moscow.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:22.615
So I think what you're seeing is

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.552
the class differences, the elite versus

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:28.488
the average people

00:06:28.488 --> 00:06:30.790
being affected by the war.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:32.091
And,

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:32.792
you know,

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.159
a certain

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.861
amount of kind of pushback,

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:37.263
even the mayor looks in

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:38.431
not very comfortable

00:06:38.431 --> 00:06:39.565
about what's going on

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:40.867
significantly Putin

00:06:40.867 --> 00:06:41.968
actually got on the phone

00:06:41.968 --> 00:06:43.770
and called him yesterday

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.538
and said, what do you need?

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.272
Again, you know,

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:48.174
trying to reassure people.

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.509
Colonel, we only have a few moments left,

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.743
but we are all waiting

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:51.778
for this counter-offensive,

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.913
of course, to start in earnest.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:54.814
Once it starts

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:55.882
with all of the new training

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.017
they've gotten, all of the new weapons

00:06:58.017 --> 00:06:58.751
that they have gotten,

00:06:58.751 --> 00:06:59.986
what are the challenges

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:01.254
that they are going to face in terms

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.722
of breaking through that Russian line

00:07:02.722 --> 00:07:03.489
and taking back

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:04.590
Russian occupied territory?

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:05.892
So during this period

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:07.293
that we've been waiting for,

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:09.362
you have all of these tank traps

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:10.029
that have been built.

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:11.664
You have all of the different

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.232
emplacements, all the trenches,

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.734
every type of thing that the Russians

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:15.768
could throw at this.

00:07:15.768 --> 00:07:16.569
They have thrown at this.

00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:17.804
So they have a very strong

00:07:17.804 --> 00:07:18.938
defensive line.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:21.107
Now, that line is only as strong

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.177
as long as the people in the Russian army

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:24.644
band.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:25.378
That line,

00:07:25.378 --> 00:07:27.313
if they're not there, if they defect,

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.981
if they retreat,

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:31.250
if they do anything like that or desert,

00:07:31.851 --> 00:07:33.619
then it's going to be a major mess.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.254
And the Ukrainians can very much

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.289
exploit that.

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:36.622
All right.

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:37.590
Well, we're still waiting for this

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.958
to start from Clayton.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.159
Jill Dougherty, thank you very much.

00:07:40.159 --> 00:07:42.028
Always appreciate your thoughts. You bet.

